g in the  entirety of the monster hunter world  that tastes sweet but i guess not  this is his first time tasting it  anyways  after these two characters start to  communicate they devised a plan to get a  sack of spider venom  to then use on the diablo to pacify it  but the plan is completely devoid of  logic  so the main character ends up baiting  herself and draws out one of the spiders  the issue with this is that all the  spiders can come out at night  since they are sensitive to the sun  because of that  the fact that only one spider comes out  to try and kill her doesn't make any  sense  especially after they end up killing the  spider more show up afterwards  like where were they before i guess it's  just oddly convenient that only one  showed up in the beginning  but besides that let's go back to the  execution of the plan  the main character must draw the spider  into a trap by running over to it  the issue with this is that the spider  just happens to be much  much faster than her to get around this  the filmmakers show us in one shot that  the spider is right about the catcher  and then in the next shot the spider is  suddenly farther away  to me this was very noticeable and  reminds me of that segment  from monty python and the holy grail  where the guy is running towards the  camera and he keeps teleporting back  whenever the camera cuts  on top of that stupid aspect there's  another one in the scene  when she ends up getting the spider to  the trap she then gets cornered and the  spider tries to impale her with its legs  but somehow the spider misses like 13  times  despite the main character hardly  dodging at all  but yeah this sequence to me is the  perfect duo of showing off plot  conveniences  and plot armor after that point in the  movie it essentially goes full blown  video game  zaniness and the main character trains  and becomes a monster hunter  to help take down the diablo because of  this it doesn't feel like the movie  takes itself very seriously anymore  this is also hammered home by the fact  that they have a cheesy training  sequence on top of a mountain  so it's harder to complain about the  different aspects in the movie by that  point  but to point out some highlights of  stupid moments later on  we have the main character being the  best rodeo champion  in the world additionally  she gets imprisoned at one point and the  lock is inside the cell  that she simply just breaks open with a  chair  more plot armor even more plot armor in  the form of surviving a helicopter crash  while being tied down  and even more plot armor from the  characters surviving an explosion  and slamming into a metal wall i don't  want to go into detail about all that  because the movie didn't seem to be  taking itself very seriously anymore  the first half of this movie to me is  much more annoying  and then the second half just goes full  tilt towards guilty pleasure craziness  because of that i feel like it's more  justified that the movie doesn't make a  lot of sense  because the tone of the movie evolves  but regardless though i hope you guys  enjoyed the video  and let me know in the comments what you  thought about the movie if you watched  it  or if i helped you dodge a bullet then  you're welcome i guess  you

